From fc699c3fd0b942384f33ee1ddc22856b8c921860 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mira <mira@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 31 May 2026 21:24:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] (be) ob-kill60 single-phase libunwind native stack
 collector
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace the stub collect step with an OceanBase-style single-phase
capture: interrupt each target thread with SIGRTMIN+6 queued via
SI_QUEUE carrying a per-request req_id in si_value.sival_ptr, seed
libunwind from the saved ucontext with UNW_INIT_SIGNAL_FRAME, walk via
unw_step / unw_get_reg, publish the frames into the per-sequence slot,
and return. The coordinator reads the slot after the handler exits;
the worker NEVER hangs waiting for the coordinator. This is the
deliberate divergence from OceanBase's upstream two-phase: OB's
ObSigHandler::handle (ob_signal_worker.cpp:349-385) writes a prepare-
ack into a pipe, blocks in wait_readable until the coordinator writes
an exit signal, then writes an exit-ack. Per docs/phase2-charter.md and
the per-variant brief, the worker-hang is OB's main open risk in our
evaluation, so ob-kill60 ships the single-phase form.

Defines UNW_LOCAL_ONLY at the TU so the include resolves to the
local-only _ULx86_64_* symbols the linked libunwind archive exposes
(the only prefix it ships). Same TU-scoped #define pattern OB uses
in ob_libunwind.c:15.

The slot ring + sequence + state machine mirror fp-walk and
ck-phdr-unwind so the safety contract is the same: the handler
validates si_pid + seq + slot state before publishing, and a
coordinator can only re-arm a slot in IDLE, so a late handler in
WALKING cannot poison the next dump. ob-kill60 needs no RBP-bounds
or junk-RBP guard because libunwind walks DWARF unwind info, not raw
frame pointers.

A defense-in-depth hasPHDRCache() check refuses to signal if the
cache is missing — without it the handler's unw_step would call the
libc dl_iterate_phdr and take the loader lock, which is not async-
signal-safe. The cache is populated by the test runner's
updatePHDRCache() call before RUN_ALL_TESTS and by doris_main after
MemInfo::init (patch 2), so this is a guard, not the normal path.

Reference: <ob>/deps/oblib/src/lib/signal/ob_signal_handlers.cpp:103-120
  (ob_signal_handler validates si_pid + req_id before dispatch),
  <ob>/deps/oblib/src/lib/signal/ob_signal_worker.cpp:280-347
  (task_process is the two-phase coordinator we collapse to single-phase),
  <ob>/deps/oblib/src/lib/signal/ob_libunwind.c:55-82
  (get_stack_trace_inplace is the unwind loop shape).
